1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,425
You change one line in your AI assistant's prompt, to fix one

2
00:00:04,425 --> 00:00:05,376
bad answer.

3
00:00:05,436 --> 00:00:09,178
That answer gets better. Three others quietly get worse.

4
00:00:09,238 --> 00:00:11,886
How would you know, before your customers do?

5
00:00:12,136 --> 00:00:14,473
Fix found: promptfoo.

6
00:00:14,533 --> 00:00:17,383
Think of it as an exam for your AI app.

7
00:00:17,443 --> 00:00:21,398
It's open source, MIT licensed, with more than twenty-six

8
00:00:21,398 --> 00:00:23,278
thousand stars on GitHub.

9
00:00:23,528 --> 00:00:27,621
You write a simple config file: your prompts, the models to try,

10
00:00:27,621 --> 00:00:29,908
and what each answer must contain.

11
00:00:29,968 --> 00:00:33,254
One command sends every test to every model.

12
00:00:33,314 --> 00:00:37,055
You get a grid of answers in your browser, each marked pass or

13
00:00:37,055 --> 00:00:37,565
fail.

14
00:00:37,815 --> 00:00:42,641
One. Compare models. Run the same tests on GPT, Claude, Gemini

15
00:00:42,641 --> 00:00:45,785
or a local model, and see which passes.

16
00:00:45,845 --> 00:00:49,613
Two. Attack your own app. Red-team mode writes hundreds of

17
00:00:49,613 --> 00:00:53,320
tricky inputs, like jailbreaks and prompt injections, and

18
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:55,083
reports what got through.

19
00:00:55,143 --> 00:00:59,228
Three. Guard every change. Run the tests automatically, so a

20
00:00:59,228 --> 00:01:03,185
prompt edit that breaks things is blocked before it ships.

21
00:01:03,435 --> 00:01:05,023
Now, the catch.

22
00:01:05,083 --> 00:01:09,557
Every test calls a real model, so big test runs mean a real API

23
00:01:09,557 --> 00:01:10,158
bill.

24
00:01:10,218 --> 00:01:14,298
Red-team attacks are generated in promptfoo's cloud by default.

25
00:01:14,298 --> 00:01:18,378
You can turn that off, but their docs say quality may drop. And

26
00:01:18,378 --> 00:01:21,423
the free version caps red teaming and sharing.

27
00:01:21,483 --> 00:01:26,154
promptfoo is now part of OpenAI, and the team says it stays open

28
00:01:26,154 --> 00:01:26,909
source.

29
00:01:27,159 --> 00:01:30,658
It's for teams shipping AI features who want to catch it when a

30
00:01:30,658 --> 00:01:32,120
change breaks something.

31
00:01:32,180 --> 00:01:35,004
For a one-off prompt, it's more than you need.

32
00:01:35,064 --> 00:01:38,524
Want an alternative? Take a look at DeepEval.

33
00:01:38,774 --> 00:01:42,970
To try it, install it, load their getting-started example, and

34
00:01:42,970 --> 00:01:47,229
add an API key. Then run the tests and open the results in your

35
00:01:47,229 --> 00:01:47,992
browser.

36
00:01:48,052 --> 00:01:51,682
What problem should we fix next? Tell us in the comments.

